{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the given addition problem in base 7, we need to determine the digits \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) such that the following equation holds:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c@{}c@{\\;}c@{}c@{}c@{}c}\n& & & & A & B_7\\\\\n&+ & & & B & A_7\\\\\n\\cline{2-6}\n& & & A & A & 0_7\\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's convert the addition problem into a base 10 equation. The number \\(ABA_7\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\nA \\cdot 7^2 + B \\cdot 7 + A = 49A + 7B + A = 50A + 7B\n\\]\n\nThe number \\(BAA_7\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\nB \\cdot 7^2 + A \\cdot 7 + A = 49B + 7A + A = 49B + 8A\n\\]\n\nThe sum of these two numbers in base 10 is:\n\\[\n50A + 7B + 49B + 8A = 58A + 56B\n\\]\n\nWe need this sum to equal the base 10 representation of \\(AAA_7\\), which is:\n\\[\nA \\cdot 7^2 + A \\cdot 7 + A = 49A + 7A + A = 57A\n\\]\n\nThus, we have the equation:\n\\[\n58A + 56B = 57A\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":790,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,2661,5256,3491,304,2331,220,22,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,18509,17767,32,57758,323,17767,33,57758,1741,429,279,2701,23606,9982,510,59,9640,59,7265,90,1653,15170,66,31,6257,66,31,35702,30031,66,31,6257,66,31,6257,66,31,6257,66,532,5,609,609,609,362,609,425,62,22,3422,198,5,10,609,609,609,425,609,362,62,22,3422,198,59,87934,90,17,12,21,532,5,609,609,362,609,362,609,220,15,62,22,3422,198,59,408,90,1653,532,59,2533,5338,11,1077,594,5508,279,5256,3491,1119,264,2331,220,16,15,23606,13,576,1372,17767,56550,62,22,57758,304,2331,220,16,15,374,510,59,9640,32,1124,50853,220,22,61,17,488,425,1124,50853,220,22,488,362,284,220,19,24,32,488,220,22,33,488,362,284,220,20,15,32,488,220,22,33,198,59,2533,785,1372,17767,33,6029,62,22,57758,304,2331,220,16,15,374,510,59,9640,33,1124,50853,220,22,61,17,488,362,1124,50853,220,22,488,362,284,220,19,24,33,488,220,22,32,488,362,284,220,19,24,33,488,220,23,32,198,59,2533,785,26